RF.put("questb:b54",{"8694":{"id":8694,"t":"Shroud of Unspoken Names","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Regal Drape, 2 Amber Idols, 5 Ivory Scarabs and 5 Bronze Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Regal Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Amber Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nShroud of Unspoken Names\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8854":{"id":8854,"t":"Twenty Signets for War Supplies","lv":49,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Horde Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8614":{"id":8614,"t":"The Horde Needs More Spotted Yellowtail!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Spotted Yellowtail to Fisherman Lin'do at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Spotted Yellowtail Raene Wolfrunner 0.7 % , Volcor 0.7 % , Terenthis 0.7 % , Sentinel Selarin 0.7 % and 4 more","desc":"So as you can see, we still be needin' a lot of the fishies. The combatants in the upcomin' Ahn'Qiraj War gonna be needin' a lot to eat, so I needin' to get all the spotted yellowtail that I can. You catch 'em, cook 'em, and bringin' 'em back to me here, and I be givin' you thanks, and the thanks of the Horde.","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"That be the best catch yet, ‹name›! Good, honest work right there. And no bones too! Thanks goin' out to you for this spotted yellowtail here mon. Come back soon if you cookin' up some more!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.1,"y":68.9,"n":"Fisherman Lin'do","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8374":{"id":8374,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,350\n+100 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"694":{"id":694,"t":"Trelane's Defenses","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find an Azure Agate and bring it to Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe.\nAzure Agate Boulderfist Shaman 20 %","desc":"All rested?\nHere's our next step: there're ogres all around the Tower of Arathor in Stromgarde. We're gonna need to activate the tower's defenses if you're gonna stand a chance against 'em an' still make it to the items alive. To do that, we're gonna need some gems the Boulderfist shaman have taken a liking to. They took 'em from the tower, but they're not gonna stay in their possession for long.\nGet one of them gems an' bring 'em to Kryten--he knows the spell to enchant 'em so they'll work as a key.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"‹name›, hello again. Have you found an azure agate yet?","done":"You amaze me, ‹name›. Well done again.\nGive me a moment to cast the proper spell to enchant the gem, an' you'll be ready.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.7,"y":47,"n":"Skuerto","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.2,"y":47.8,"n":"Apprentice Kryten","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"4134":{"id":4134,"t":"Lost Thunderbrew Recipe","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Lost Thunderbrew Recipe to Vivian Lagrave in Kargath.\nLost Thunderbrew Recipe Blackbreath Crony , Hurley Blackbreath","desc":"It is rumored that the Dark Iron Hurley Blackbreath has stolen a recipe for ale. This ale, Thunderbrew Lager, is said to infuse its imbiber with great strength and courage. We wish to study the drink. Perhaps, we will find other applications for its virtues... applications more in line with Forsaken objectives.\nDelve into Blackrock Depths, find Hurley, take from him the recipe for Thunderbrew lager and bring it to me.\nAnd to find him, you may have to entice him by threatening his precious ale.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwiftstrike Cudgel Limb Cleaver\nYou will also receive:\n5 Superior Healing Potion 5 Greater Mana Potion\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650","back":"Do you have the recipe for the Thunderbrew Lager, ‹name›?","done":"Very good. I will send this recipe to the Apothecarium to be studied, and in time we will unlock its secrets. One day, the dwarves of the Alliance may find the virtues of this drink used against them!\nI find that terribly amusing. Perhaps death has an affect on one's sense of humor... do you think?","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"7654":{"id":7654,"t":"Imperial Plate Boots","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"40 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Boots\n+150 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"For the boot plans, I'll be needin' 40 thorium bars. Yep, 40. Are you gonna cry? Would you like a hanky?\n<Derotain laughs.>","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"94294":{"id":94294,"t":"Craftsmans writ dusky bracers","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Dusky Bracers\nDusky Bracers","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Dusky Bracers, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Dusky Bracers Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94294","cats":["crafting"]},"94214":{"id":94214,"t":"Craftsmans writ shadow protection potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Shadow Protection Potion\nShadow Protection Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Shadow Protection Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Heyo, for future reference, you shouldn't come charging at full-speed toward a goblin with a bodyguard! You never know what might happen.","done":"Then again, when you're fulfilling a rush order like this one, I can't blame you for wanting to capitalize on your gains.\nHere you go, pal. Thanks for hooking a goblin up with some much-needed shadow protection potions. Have you SEEN the stuff that goes on out here?","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":81.7,"y":19.9,"n":"Kzixx","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7894":{"id":7894,"t":"Copper Modulator","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Copper Modulator Arcane Nullifier X-21 8 % , Crawler 7.5 % , Foe Reaper 4000 4.8 % , Mobile Alert System 2.9 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nDarkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"Yebb is developing a new attraction for the Zoo Bizarre, one that will drive people crazy with wonder, and delight! But it will take a lot of work, and a lot of materials...\nThat includes copper modulators. We need lots of modulators for the mechanical parts of the attraction. Bring me copper modulators and I'll trade for them with a Darkmoon Faire ticket.","done":"Aha! The modulators! Superb!\nI can't tell you exactly what we're building, but these will be invaluable for its construction. I am in your debt, Grimling, but please, take this Darkmoon Faire ticket as a token of my appreciation.\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38,"y":44.3,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":70.7,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"97894":{"id":97894,"t":"Business in auberdine","lv":17,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Check on Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine in Darkshore.\nBorgus mentioned a boat on the southern-most dock in Stormwind Harbor that can take you there.\nTake the boat to Auberdine and find Gorbold Steelhand.","desc":"Pleasure to make yer acquaintance! Name's Borgus, of the one and only Steelhand family. You can always count on a Steelhand fer a fair deal!\nA few weeks back me brother Gorbold joined up with a merchant stall in Auberdine. Plenty of coin to be made supplyin' ships there, let me tell you! Lucky sod.\nI haven't heard from him since--mind checking on him if yer heading that way?\nThere's a new ship in the harbor that will take ye straight there. Head to the southern-most dock; can't miss it!","done":"Old Borgy sent you? Always looking out for me.\nWe could certainly use another set of hands around here. Business has all but stopped with the recent tragedy, and I think you could help set things right.\nStormwind City Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.4,"y":12.6,"n":"Borgus Steelhand","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":38,"y":41.2,"n":"Gorbold Steelhand","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6134":{"id":6134,"t":"Ghost-o-plasm Round Up","lv":39,"min":34,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Ghost-o-plasms and the Crate of Ghost Magnets to Hornizz Brimbuzzle in Desolace.\nCrate of Ghost Magnets\n8 Ghost-o-plasm Magrami Spectre 80 %\nProvided: Crate of Ghost Magnets","desc":"There's a valley to the southeast, the Valley of Bones, haunted by Magram ghosts. Sounds scary, doesn't it? Well think how scary it is to the Magram! If we captured ghost energy from that place, I bet it'd be worth plenty to those centaurs.\nHere, take this crate of ghost magnets. If you place one between the two big skeletons in the valley, the Dead Goliaths, then ghosts will wander to it. Distance yourself, take out the ghosts and get their ghost-o-plasm--that's what we'll sell to the Magram.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCondor Bracers Anchorhold Buckler\nMoney: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,250","back":"Where's my ghost-o-plasm, ‹name›?","done":"There it is! Looks like you got some of it on you too. Kinda slimey, eh?\nWell, thanks a lot for all the trouble, ‹name›. This stuff will be worth a fortune... if I can convince the centaurs what it is!\nDesolace Shen'dralas","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":47.8,"y":61.8,"n":"Hornizz Brimbuzzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7494":{"id":7494,"t":"Feathermoon Stronghold","lv":57,"min":54,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Latronicus Moonspear at the Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.","desc":"‹name›! Your aid is needed in Feralas!\nAn outlaw mage, Lethtendris, has fled to the ancient elven ruins Eldre'thalas, now called Dire Maul. It is believed she has an item of dangerous magical energy which must be recovered.\nLatronicus Moonspear requests agents to enter Dire Maul and retrieve the item from Lethtendris.\nServe the Alliance! Seek out Latronicus at the Feathermoon Stronghold in Feralas.","rew":"Experience: 1,500","done":"Hail, ‹name›. I am pleased to see you, but regret that our meeting is not under more pleasant conditions.\nListen close, for I have a vital task for you...\nStormwind City Dun Morogh Darnassus Feralas","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":56.4,"y":74.1,"n":"Crier Goodman","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":60.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Courier Hammerfall","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":47.8,"y":82,"n":"Herald Moonstalker","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":30.4,"y":46.2,"n":"Latronicus Moonspear","e":1}],"cats":["dire-maul"]},"3094":{"id":3094,"t":"Verdant Note","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 40 experience instead of 50, 0.8 times as much.","obj":"Read the Verdant Note and speak to Gart Mistrunner in Camp Narache.\nVerdant Note\nProvided: Verdant Note","desc":"Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, ‹name›. I believe she was sent by the druid trainer Gart. If this note is from Gart, I wouldn't take long in reading its contents.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"You have arrived. This is good. Our ancestors' spirits have become restless throughout Mulgore and beyond, but I cannot tell why. It will forever be your duty to learn to listen to nature's spirits, and act as their avatar. Be mindful of that.","done":"Though we share a common bond, do not expect much welcome from the night elves. Their pride still limits their sight, but that is none of our concern. The teachings of the Earthmother are all you must concern yourself with, and I will teach you what I know as you grow in wisdom.\nReturn to me often, ‹name›. You will find that the Earthmother grants incredible abilities to those who are most dedicated.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.6,"y":76.6,"n":"Gart Mistrunner","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"134":{"id":134,"t":"Ogre Thieves","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Abercrombie's Crate to Abercrombie.\nAbercrombie's Crate Abercrombie's Crate , Abercrombie's Crate","desc":"A few weeks ago I was picking herbs far from my house, and a band of ogres attacked me! I ran, and I was forced to leave behind a crate of precious tools and herbs.\nAfter they chased me off, the ogres swaggered back to the ogre mound in southern Duskwood. I'm sure my crate is somewhere near the mound.\nPlease, ‹name›, retrieve this crate for me for I miss it sorely.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,200","back":"Do you have my crate? If so, then please...give it to me quickly!","done":"Thank the Nec-...well, thank YOU, ‹name›! You have more than earned your reward.\nAha! Happy! Happy nights ahead!!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"54":{"id":54,"t":"Report to Goldshire","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Marshal McBride's Documents to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire.\nMarshal McBride's Documents\nProvided: Marshal McBride's Documents","desc":"‹name›, you are a ‹class› with proven interest in the security of Northshire. You are now tasked with the protection of the surrounding Elwynn Forest.\nIf you accept this duty, then I have prepared papers that must be delivered to Marshal Dughan in Goldshire. Goldshire lies along the southern road, past the border gates.","rew":"You will receive:\nPikeman Shield\nExperience: 230\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You have word from McBride? Northshire is a garden compared to Elwynn Forest, but I wonder what Marshal McBride has to report.\nHere, let me have his papers...","done":"Well, it says here that you've been awarded Acting Deputy Status with the Stormwind Marshals. Congratulations.\nAnd good luck - keeping Elwynn safe is no picnic... what with most the army busy doing who knows what for who knows which noble!\nIt's hard to keep track of politics in these dark days...","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.9,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":42.1,"y":65.9,"n":"Marshal Dughan","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"7734":{"id":7734,"t":"Improved Quality","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Rage Scar Yeti Hides to Jangdor Swiftstrider at Camp Mojache, Feralas.\n10 Rage Scar Yeti Hide Lurking Feral Scar , Ferocious Rage Scar 70 % , Elder Rage Scar 70 % , Rage Scar Yeti 70 %","desc":"I have a lead on an even BETTER source of hides, if that's even possible to believe! In the northern parts of Feralas - deep within Rage Scar Hold - are another throng of yetis. They're much tougher than the ones you dealt with before, so if you're up for a bigger challenge you'd best be on your toes!\nI would reward you handsomely for a stack of ten of their hides; bring them to me here, and we'll finish our business.","rew":"You will receive:\nJangdor's Handcrafted Tunic\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"If these Rage Scar yeti hides are anything like the quality displayed by their Feral Scar counterparts, they could very well be as resilient as thorium!\nImagine that!","done":"Excellent, excellent! These are going to work out incredibly well - I can already tell that they're going to be much harder when properly cured.\nThanks again for your aid, ‹name›. Here - please take one of my latest creations.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"9094":{"id":9094,"t":"Argent Dawn Gloves","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 55.","obj":"30 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGloves of Undead Cleansing Handwraps of Undead Slaying Handguards of Undead Slaying Gauntlets of Undead Slaying","back":"If you bring me thirty necrotic runes, I will give you your choice of hand protection in return. These should prove valuable in our fight against the undead Scourge.","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. Take your pick of hand protection in thanks for your efforts.\nDun Morogh Stormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.8,"y":30.7,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":72.6,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.1,"y":45.4,"n":"Argent Quartermaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"9334":{"id":9334,"t":"Blessed Wizard Oil","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 0.","obj":"8 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nBlessed Wizard Oil","back":"In exchange for the necrotic runes of the Scourge invaders, the Argent Dawn will give you one vial of blessed wizard oil.","done":"I hope that you will find these items useful in future battles.\nUndercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65,"y":45.6,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.1,"y":58.5,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8934":{"id":8934,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Devout Belt and a set of Devout Gloves to Deliana in Ironforge.\nDevout Belt Blackhand Summoner 7.6 % , Smolderthorn Shadow Priest 4.4 % , Firebrand Dreadweaver 4.3 % , Scarshield Spellbinder 2 % and 2 more\nDevout Gloves Archivist Galford 0 % in Stratholme","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gloves that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","rew":"You will receive:\nVirtuous Belt Virtuous Gloves\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2854":{"id":2854,"t":"Wild Leather Armor","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Leather to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n10 Thick Leather Razzashi Cobra 37.5 % in Zul'Gurub , Felsteel Chest 7.1 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 4.5 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 4.5 % and 4 more","desc":"‹name›, your skill as a leatherworker precedes you. I possess leatherworking lore you would be wise to acquire... Wild Leather armor! Wild Leather taps into the potent and chaotic properties of wildvines, found in areas of lush vegetation and on some of the creatures there. Armor made using it is second to none for a crafter of your skill, guaranteed.\nI'll teach you, but you'll be working for me for a while. The first cost is simply ten pieces of thick leather. After this, we'll talk specifics.","rew":"Experience: 1,950","back":"We must be clear; you shall be apprenticed to me while you learn the art of Wild Leather armor. Because wildvines are both potent and chaotic, it yields a random but strong benefit to the already strong armor you will be making. This knowledge, however, was not easy for me to acquire.\nThe initial cost to begin this process is ten pieces of thick leather.\nOnce that is done, we'll get to the work you need to do in order to obtain the patterns.","done":"Well ‹name›, I'm glad to have you on board as my apprentice. You've made a wise decision as a leatherworker; those who make use of leather armor will be clamoring to you once you learn how to master the art of Wild Leather.\nLet's get to work - where do you want to start?","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"454":{"id":454,"t":"After the Ambush","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Miran.","desc":"We'd been hauling the barrels of powder back and forth in trips before this... business. Now we have to split up the work, Miran's taking the barrels and I'm watching over the other ones.\nI don't feel safe letting Miran haul the rest of the shipment by himself. When he's ready to go, maybe you could escort him on his next trip?","rew":"Experience: 110\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","done":"Hello, ‹class›.\nYou'll be escorting me to the excavation site? That's good to hear... After Saean and his cronies, who knows what else the Dark Irons might have up their sleeves?\nAnyways, let me just make some final checks. Talk to me again when you're ready to go.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":52.2,"y":69.3,"n":"Huldar","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":52.2,"y":69.4,"n":"Miran","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"86614":{"id":86614,"t":"Silver of the waves","lv":20,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return the Monogrammed Silver Hair clip to its owner.\nProvided: Monogrammed Silver Hair Clip","desc":"<Among the fishing knickknacks in the debris are some rusty hooks, broken spools of wire, and a slightly corroded but ornate silver hair clip with the monogram \"K.D.\">","rew":"You will receive:\nRepurposed Hair Band\nMoney: 12 0 gold, 12 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I have a lot of chores today, so can you keep it quick?","done":"My hair clip! I thought this was lost for good!\nThis'll shine right up with just a little work. Thank you for bringing it to me! I'll make it worth your while.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":48,"y":39.7,"n":"Discarded Fishing Toolbox","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":40.4,"y":39.4,"n":"Khara Deepwater","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"854":{"id":854,"t":"Journey to the Crossroads","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Thork at the Crossroads in the Barrens.","desc":"I have foreseen your arrival, young ‹class›. Though perhaps you are not so young anymore.\nI think that it is time for you to move deeper into this land. I can sense that you are destined for great things.\nIt is the Crossroads that you must seek out, for our lives with the orcs have become intertwined and they need assistance. Continue down this road towards the east and follow it north to the Crossroads. Find Thork within its walls, he has the Earthmother's blessing.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"It is good to see that more of our ‹race› allies have come to assist us from as far away as Thunder Bluff. Again, I welcome you.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":58.6,"n":"Kirge Sternhorn","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.5,"y":30.9,"n":"Thork","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"96294":{"id":96294,"t":"A darker truth","lv":30,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the letter you recovered from Broodmother Valraxx to Muln Earthfury at Skywatcher Plateau.\nProvided: Bloody Parchment","desc":"<The Broodmother you just killed is no spider at all, but rather a night elf druid who assumed a twisted animal form. A variety of questions flood your mind about the nature--and purpose--of the spiders at Gloomrise.\nYou notice a note peeking out of the folds of the dead elf's robe. Perhaps this document may answer some of the questions filling your head.>","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,850\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Muln Earthfury","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"96774":{"id":96774,"t":"Ancient gurubashi idol","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover an Ancient Gurubashi Idol from the Drowned City.\nAncient Gurubashi Idol","desc":"The ancient Gurubashi of Stranglethorn Vale were da masters of dark blood magics. Rumors be they'd use pure truesilver idols to channel that bad bad voodoo.\nOl' Mazu'kon would love to get his hands on one of those idols... for academics ya see. How 'bout you gather some friends and do a bit of smash and grab on that drowned city stickin' out the ocean off the coast of Stranglethorn? Kill the most impressive lookin' priest ya can find in there, and they sure to have what I be lookin' for.","rew":"Money: 1 1 gold, 0 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,800\n+300 reputation with Earthen Ring\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":32.4,"y":20.6,"n":"Mazu'kon","s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9014":{"id":9014,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Magister's Crown and Magister's Robes.\nMagister's Crown Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nMagister's Robes General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nSorcerer's Crown Sorcerer's Robes\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Magister's pieces in exchange for your new Sorcerer's Crown and Robes?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1654":{"id":1654,"t":"The Test of Righteousness","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 875 experience instead of 2,200, 0.4 times as much.","obj":"Using Jordan's Weapon Notes, find some Whitestone Oak Lumber, Bailor's Refined Ore Shipment, Jordan's Smithing Hammer, and a Kor Gem, and return them to Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge.\nWhitestone Oak Lumber Goblin Woodcarver in The Deadmines\nJordan's Refined Ore Shipment\nJordan's Smithing Hammer Jordan's Hammer in Shadowfang Keep\nPurified Kor Gem\nProvided: Jordan's Weapon Notes","desc":"I'd like to reward you if you'd be willing to accept such a thing? Don't misunderstand me, my generosity is dependent on how much help you can be, but I see us both benefiting greatly from such an alliance.\nI will craft for you a weapon worthy of what you've accomplished, a symbol of paladinhood and the Light, but you must gather the items I need to craft it. I've already started taking notes on the items, it just requires someone brave and skilled enough to recover them. What do you say, ‹class›?","rew":"Experience: 875","back":"The items you're seeking will be difficult to acquire, but I can assure you, the weapon I will craft for you will be worth the effort.\nIt will be my finest work to date, and only a small payment for the service you've done me.","done":"This is wonderful! You've gotten all the items.\nI should have no problem forging you a grand weapon with these. I've actually had the plans for doing this for some time. I just never had the opportunity to gather the goods. Thank you, ‹name›.\nIt feels good to have my father's hammer again...and a Kor gem. I never thought I'd see one of these myself.\nDun Morogh Loch Modan Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":52.5,"y":36.9,"n":"Jordan Stilwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94774":{"id":94774,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"You've caught the attention of our superiors, ‹name›. They've asked you travel to the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Laurena. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, Ander. There are many things we will have to discuss, but more importantly is your training in the ways of the Light.\nThere are lessons all servants of the Light must learn. If you are ready, we'll begin discussing some of those now.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.4,"y":65.6,"n":"Priestess Josetta","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"5654":{"id":5654,"t":"Hex of Weakness","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Ur'kyo in Orgrimmar.","desc":"It be time for you to meet with Ur'kyo, ‹name›. He be in the Valley of Spirits in the orc city. Go there and speak to him. It is time you learn more of the old ways of our kind. It time you be brought into the circle and made a true priest of our tribe.","rew":"You will learn: Hex of Weakness\nExperience: 210","done":"You would do well to pay heed to this lesson, young one. The Hex of Weakness will be a great boon to you in battle. Later I will have tests for you to further yourself and prove your worth to the tribe.\nMulgore Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.2,"y":62.3,"n":"Var'jun","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":35.6,"y":87.8,"n":"Ur'kyo","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"1014":{"id":1014,"t":"Arugal Must Die","lv":27,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,850 experience instead of 3,300, 2.68 times as much. Read from what the game server sent.","obj":"Kill Arugal and bring his head to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\nHead of Arugal Archmage Arugal in Shadowfang Keep","desc":"Arugal still resides in Shadowfang Keep. We cannot claim Silverpine as a strategic stronghold for the Dark Lady until Arugal is slain.\nI shall see to it that his magic is eradicated, ‹name›. But I leave it in your hands to see that Arugal meets the death he so deserves.\nTravel to Shadowfang Keep and put an end to Arugal's foul spells once and for all. Bring to me the vile wizard's head!","rew":"You will receive:\nSeal of Sylvanas\nExperience: 8,850\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"With Arugal's death we stand to increase the Dark Lady's stronghold on Lordaeron.","done":"Silverpine Forest is finally free from the vice of that wretch Arugal. You have done the Dark Lady a great service, ‹name›. Your tenacity shall be rewarded.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shadowfang-keep"]},"94374":{"id":94374,"t":"Call of earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Spirit Stone and drink the Earth Sapta.\nEarth Sapta","desc":"Aye, sapta's a brew forged with magic, bindin' our spirit to the elements. Only a few shaman know the recipe, and it's nae for the weak-willed. Drink it, and ye will see what others can't. Hold true--it's only to be drunk in a sacred place.\nHead north to the Spirit Stone, tucked at the end of a hidden path up the mountain. Drink it there... see what the earth has to show ye.","done":"Ah... Thordin... the earth welcomes you, even in this frozen land. Bound in body and spirit, you'll walk forward knowing the mountains are your strength, the plains your patience, and the world your essence.\nTo pass this rite, stand humbly before the earth. The other elements are not so still - they clash and roar. Learn their dual nature, even here among the snow and stone.\nDun Morogh Durotar Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.1,"n":"Teo Hammerstorm","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":44,"y":76,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":53.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8534":{"id":8534,"t":"Hive'Zora Scout Report","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Contact Cenarion Scout Azenel inside Hive'Zora and return the Hive'Zora Scout Report to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold. You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\nHive'Zora Scout Report\nTactical Task Briefing VI\nProvided: Tactical Task Briefing VI","desc":"We've sent our best scouts deep into the silithid hives to gather intelligence. Scout Azenel has been watching the silithid movements at Hive'Zora for several days now. Find her and obtain a written report. We need to be able to act on that information as soon as possible, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Tactical Badge Followup Tactical Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You'll find Scout Azenel inside Hive'Zora. Hurry, ‹name›! Time is of the essence.","done":"Your efforts are greatly appreciated, ‹name›. I'll read these scouting reports right away, feel free to go over your next assignment.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Windcaller Proudhorn","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8774":{"id":8774,"t":"Target: Hive'Regal Ambushers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 30 Hive'Regal Ambushers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing VIII in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing VIII\nHive'Regal Ambusher slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing VIII","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Regal where your primary target will consist of the Hive'Regal ambushers.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You wish to tell me something, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Your part in the attack on Hive'Regal has been noted.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79094":{"id":79094,"t":"The lessons of tazo","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"The Lessons of Ta'zo","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nThe Lessons of Ta'zo (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1094":{"id":1094,"t":"Further Instructions","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Sealed Envelope to Sputtervalve in the Barrens.\nSealed Envelope\nProvided: Sealed Envelope","desc":"This envelope has all the information I was able to snatch as they booted me out the door... Venture Company internal documents, some manuals, technical things... Oh, and of course the Super Reaper 6000 blueprints.\nSputtervalve has taken up residence at Ratchet in the Barrens. Shouldn't have much trouble finding him, he's a little green fellow.","rew":"Experience: 825\n+50 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Hello there! How can I help you?","done":"Fizziks, eh? Can't say I trust him, but this information seems good enough. What I wouldn't give to have the Venture Company out of my hair.\nThey do come up with some good machines though... I can't deny that we've benefited from using some of the improvements they've devised.\nStonetalon Mountains The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"79974":{"id":79974,"t":"Wet job","lv":32,"min":14,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Dusting off a messenger bag emerging from the soil, you find a parchment nestled among the supplies.","desc":"\"Always like to keep a reserve stash nearby in the off chance I've got to flee in a hurry.\nThe face of this mountainside is so beautiful you might say it was carved from the waterfalls of time.\nThat's the eagles nest, that's what you're looking for.\"","rew":"You will receive:\nHickory Pipe Rumsey Rum Light\nExperience: 2,550","done":"Dwarven Engineering, always a marvel.\nStonetalon Mountains Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":39.6,"y":49.9,"n":"Mound of Dirt","s":1},{"z":"Loch Modan","x":49.5,"y":12.8,"n":"Carved Figurine","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"614":{"id":614,"t":"The Captain's Chest","lv":47,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 47 instead of 51. Gives 3,150 experience instead of 4,800, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring Smotts' Chest to Hecklebury Smotts in Booty Bay.\nSmotts' Chest Gorlash","desc":"I used to sail a ship from here all the way to Ratchet, in Kalimdor. I was a successful captain with a sterling reputation.\nUntil...\nThose cursed sea giants ruined me! They smashed my ship, killed my crew, and set me on a lifeboat to Booty Bay. And one of the giants, Gorlash, stole my Captain's Chest. He said he wanted it for a snuffbox. The nerve!\nI hear Gorlash wanders the coast east of here. Find him and get back my chest! Do that, and you'll have earned a captain's gratitude.","rew":"You will receive:\nBloodband Bracers\nExperience: 3,150\n+75 reputation with Booty Bay\n-375 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Ahoy, ‹name›! Did you find Gorlash? That chest was my favorite, and it has a hidden compartment that held my greatest treasures!","done":"You found it! Oh happy day, this is! Thank you, ‹name›. Getting back my chest cools some of the fire in me.\nBut my revenge isn't complete...\nStranglethorn Vale Open the zone on the world map Level 47 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 43 45 50 59 Side Alliance Type Elite Shareable Yes Quest ID 614","cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8054":{"id":8054,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Freethinker's Belt","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 61. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Shawl. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Shawl\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"Your beliefs are alien to us, heathen. Ancient Zandalar were once branded as heretics. This was when the Gurubashi Empire was strong. Heathens dared to challenge the priest of Hakkar. Heathens then were hunted and killed as vermin. Those heathens never wavered in their fight against the Blood God. We honor the price they paid. They are the freethinkers.\nDestroy the minions of Hakkar in Zul'Gurub. Bring me the Paragons of Power I seek. Success will be greatly rewarded.\nGo.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Freethinker's Belt\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Your presence means victory? Do you have the Paragons? Are you dripping in the remains of your enemies?","done":"Your honor is assured in the tribe. You claim many deaths in Zul'Gurub. Enemies fall before your convictions. Enemies fall before your power.\nThis is the freethinker's belt. It is a symbol of honor. It is powerful mojo. It is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"934":{"id":934,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":11,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Amethyst Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nVial of Blessed Water\nProvided: Amethyst Phial","desc":"All was not well with Teldrassil, however. Staghelm's carefully made plans for the new World Tree had borne out as he had hoped, but there was one small problem, a problem to which many of the troubles on Teldrassil may be attributed.\nHowever, I will not get into that yet. You must visit the last moonwell, to the northwest in the Oracle Glade. Under the boughs of the Oracle Tree lies the first and most powerful of our wells. Retrieve a phial of its water and return to me.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Along with the druids, the Oracle Tree and the Arch Druid have been carefully monitoring the growth of Teldrassil. But though we have a new home, our immortal lives have not been restored.","done":"To be in the presence of the Oracle Tree... it is almost to feel wisdom take form. Let me continue the telling...\nWith Teldrassil grown, the Arch Druid approached the dragons for their blessings, as the dragons had placed upon Nordrassil in ancient times. But Nozdormu, Lord of Time, refused to give his blessing, chiding the druid for his arrogance. In agreement with Nozdormu, Alexstrasza also refused Staghelm, and without her blessing, Teldrassil's growth has been flawed and unpredictable...\nLevel 11 , requires level 1 The quest before it, Webwood Venom, requires level 3. Difficulty 1 7 9 14 17 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 934\nThe chain\n9 quests from level 4 to 11, 4,390 XP in all.\n1 [ 4 ] Webwood Venom\nBring 10 Webwood Venom Sacs to Gilshalan Windwalker at Aldrassil.\nGilshalan Windwalker Teldrassil\n360 XP\n2 [ 5 ] Webwood Egg\nBring a Webwood Egg to Gilshalan in Aldrassil.\nGilshalan Windwalker Teldrassil\n550 XP\n3 [ 5 ] Tenaron's Summons\nSpeak with Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil in Shadowglen.\nGilshalan Windwalker Teldrassil\n45 XP\n4 [ 5 ] Crown of the Earth\nFill the Crystal Phial and bring it back to Tenaron Stormgrip atop Aldrassil.\nTenaron Stormgrip Teldrassil\n340 XP\n5 [ 5 ] Crown of the Earth\nBring the Partially Filled Vessel to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nTenaron Stormgrip Teldrassil\n230 XP\n6 [ 5 ] Crown of the Earth\nFill the Jade Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nCorithras Moonrage Teldrassil\n340 XP\n7 [ 9 ] Crown of the Earth\nFill the Tourmaline Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nCorithras Moonrage Teldrassil\n775 XP\n8 [ 11 ] Crown of the Earth this quest\nFill the Amethyst Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\n650 XP\n9 [ 11 ] Crown of the Earth\nBring the Filled Vessel to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\nCorithras Moonrage Teldrassil\n1,100 XP","cats":["teldrassil"]},"95494":{"id":95494,"t":"Bruised pride and lion hides","lv":18,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 Savannah Lion Hides from the Savannah Matriarchs and Savannah Patriarchs in the Barrens.\n6 Savannah Lion Hide","desc":"I need someone with a strong sword arm and some extra time on their hands to help me gather some lion hides. It stings my pride to ask a stranger for this aid, but I took an injury to my leg recently. Until I heal, I'm in no shape to go hunting myself but I have obligations to keep.\nThe big ones in this area generally have the best hides, so start with those first.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes the hunt?","done":"Yes, these look like they will do nicely. I have an arrangement with a local tanner to deliver these raw hides in exchange for various finished leather goods that I use as part of my trade.\nI've never come up short on my end of the arrangement, and even with my injury I do not intend to start now.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":43.8,"y":12.2,"n":"Vrang Wildgore","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"214":{"id":214,"t":"Red Silk Bandanas","lv":17,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,950 experience instead of 1,250, 2.36 times as much. New rewards: Monastic Hammer. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a nor","obj":"Scout Riell at the Sentinel Hill Tower wants you to bring her 10 Red Silk Bandanas.\n10 Red Silk Bandana Defias Wizard 80 % in The Deadmines , Defias Taskmaster 80 % in The Deadmines , Defias Strip Miner 80 % in The Deadmines , Defias Squallshaper 80 % in The Deadmines and 4 more","desc":"It's no secret that the trademark of the Defias Gang is their Red Bandanas. But we've learned that the material from which these bandanas are made signifies the member's rank.\nThat being said, I want you to eliminate as many high ranking Defias members as you can. The highest ranking members will undoubtedly be found in VanCleef's secret hideout. When you're done bring me 10 Red Silk Bandanas as proof of their deaths and I will reward you. Good luck, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSolid Shortblade Scrimshaw Dagger Piercing Axe Monastic Hammer\nNew in Forever: Monastic Hammer.\nExperience: 2,950\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you been reclaiming our land from the Defias gang? If so show me 10 Red Silk Bandanas as proof.","done":"Well done, ‹name›! On behalf of The People's Militia I salute you for your efforts. Soon we will return this land to the people with help from brave souls like you.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.7,"y":47.3,"n":"Scout Riell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-deadmines"]},"2934":{"id":2934,"t":"Undamaged Venom Sac","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring an Undamaged Venom Sac to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill.\nUndamaged Venom Sac Witherbark Broodguard 10 %","desc":"I must have a fresh sample of the venom you brought me. The spiders from which it was gathered must dwell in the Hinterlands -- hunt them until you find an undamaged venom sac and bring it to me. You will find many spiders near the troll city of Shadra'Alor.\nDo not tarry, ‹name›, for the venom sac must be fresh when you deliver it.","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do you have the undamaged venom sac, ‹name›? I yearn to run experiments with its fresh venom, and have ordered a collection of small, terribly cute animals on which to test it!","done":"Oh, splendid! The venom is quite fresh and I'm sure very deadly. Thank you!\nHillsbrad Foothills The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"1174":{"id":1174,"t":"Gnomes win","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Gnome Race Ticket","rew":"You will receive:\nGnome Prize Box\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 1174","cats":["thousand-needles"]},"374":{"id":374,"t":"Proof of Demise","lv":7,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Scarlet Insignia Rings to Deathguard Burgess in Brill.\n10 Scarlet Insignia Ring Captain Melrache 40 % , Captain Vachon 40 % , Captain Perrine 40 % , Scarlet Bodyguard 40 % and 4 more","desc":"Executor Zygand tells me you've been out killing Scarlet Crusaders. Tirisfal Glades is crawling with them.\nVarimathras, lieutenant to The Dark Lady, is seeing to it personally that the scum of Azeroth, the Human race, gets wiped into oblivion. Here in Tirisfal Glades we face a particularly annoying breed of humans: The Scarlet Crusade.\nVenture forth and wage an offensive on the Scarlet Crusade, ‹class›. Bring me back 10 Scarlet Insignia Rings as proof of your loyalty to Varimathras and The Dark Lady.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nZombie Skin Bracers Clasped Belt Netted Gloves\nMoney: 1 75 0 gold, 1 silver, 75 copper Experience: 625\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you collected 10 Scarlet Insignia Rings yet, ‹class›?","done":"Varimathras would be proud. You serve your leaders well, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.9,"y":52,"n":"Deathguard Burgess","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"4294":{"id":4294,"t":"... and a Batch of Ooze","lv":56,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather Un'Goro Slime Samples from any of the slimes in Un'Goro Crater. Then, using the Testing Equipment next to Chemist Fuely in Undercity, see which of your samples are the most pure. Bring 5 of the Pure Un'Goro Samples you find to Chemist Fuely.\n5 Pure Un'Goro Sample","desc":"Have you heard of the Un'Goro Crater, ‹name›? It is near the Tanaris desert, and it is a magnificent place: lush, vibrant, full of creatures and plant life.\nIt is there you must go. Word has reached me that the place seems completely untainted by outside hands. Explorers are just now discovering its secrets.\nI would like to test the slimes or oozes there. If it is true--that they are uncorrupt--then I would like to see how such creatures have evolved.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes, ‹name›? How goes your search?","done":"Truly amazing, ‹name›. This Un'Goro Crater is holding many more secrets than I expected. I wonder what else we will discover as we test further.\nSimply amazing... look at the purity of these samples. Hmm, I wonder what it could mean. They seem to be elemental in nature, but... something more. They remind me of... of the Old Gods. We've found traces of them throughout Azeroth, and now I wonder if these creatures aren't related to them somehow.\nWe shall have to test further.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":47.5,"y":73.3,"n":"Chemist Fuely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"7814":{"id":7814,"t":"A Donation of Silk","lv":60,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Silk Cloth Protector Weaver , Mountaineer Langarr 85.7 % , Watcher Wollpert 85.7 % , Mountaineer Zwarn 78.3 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"As with most other fabrics, our stocks of silk are at an all-time low. Our stores are such that we'd only need sixty pieces of silk from you total; we should be able to reach our goal with the support of others.\nA benevolent gift such as silk, might I add, would certainly increase your local standing in the community! If you have the sixty pieces of silk cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":71.7,"y":29.2,"n":"Ralston Farnsley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"8294":{"id":8294,"t":"Quell the Silverwing Usurpers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Enter Warsong Gulch and defeat the Alliance, gain a Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor, and bring it to Captain Shatterskull at the Mor'shan Base Camp.\nWarsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The wilds of the Ashenvale forest will succumb to the might of the Horde, ‹race›. Nothing the Silverwing say or do can stop our sovereign imperative. Kalimdor belongs to the Horde. How dare they attempt to prevent us from harvesting what is rightfully ours!\nLet the pride swell in your chest as you cut down their weak attempts at slowing our progress. Destroy the Silverwing Sentinels, and earn a Warsong mark of honor. Return to me with such a mark, ‹name›, and you will be rewarded.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders\n+200 reputation with Warsong Outriders","back":"The blood of our enemies is a mark of honor. Do you have such a mark?","done":"<Captain Shatterskull roars in triumph.>\nHow much more can they withstand? How many more Alliance filth must perish at the hands of the Horde for them to retreat? Only time will tell, ‹race›.\nLevel 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Orc, Undead, Tauren, Troll Type PvP Shareable No Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8294","cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"5094":{"id":5094,"t":"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out High Executor Derrington. His base camp is located at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glade and the Undercity.","desc":"Heroes of the realm, hear me - the Horde calls upon you for swift action!\nA call to arms has been issued for all able bodied individuals to take up arms against the Scourge! Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Eastern Kingdoms. They loom to the east of the Undercity, in the northern reaches of the lands now known as the Plaguelands!\nHeroes of the realm - seek out High Executor Derrington, who has set up his base camp at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glade!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, with the looming threat of the Scourge to our east, and then even further still eastward from there. I am glad to hear that the call of duty and service to the Horde did not fall on deaf ears with you!\nIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":63.9,"y":44.1,"n":"Harbinger Balthazad","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"294":{"id":294,"t":"Ormer's Revenge","lv":24,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ormer Ironbraid at the Whelgar Excavation Site wants you to kill 10 Mottled Screechers and 10 Mottled Raptors.\nMottled Raptor slain : 0/ 10\nMottled Screecher slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The situation is severe, that much is for sure. When we uncovered these bones it attracted the Raptors. These filthy beasts killed my brethren and trapped me, Merrin and the poor Prospector up here.\nHelp clear the Wetlands of these Raptors, ‹name›. Mottled Raptors and Mottled Screechers are just West of the bluff there. Kill 10 of each, if you can.\nThat will be a good start to the vengeance I have planned for them.","rew":"Money: 17 0 gold, 17 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Kill 10 Mottled Raptors and 10 Mottled Screechers, ‹name›. My co-workers did not deserve the fate that was brought upon them. It's time to even the score.","done":"Killing is a dirty business, but you did your job well, ‹name›. If I weren't obligated to stay with the Prospector and Merrin, I'd be down there shedding blood right along side you.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.2,"y":50.9,"n":"Ormer Ironbraid","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"92454":{"id":92454,"t":"Welcome","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Thendal Grove Gift Voucher to Dalia Windbreeze.\nProvided: Thendal Grove Gift Voucher","desc":"Welcome to the World of Warcraft!\nAs special thanks for purchasing the World of Warcraft Collector's Edition, turn in this gift voucher to Dalia Windbreeze in Thendal Grove. You'll then be given a gift: a little companion to join you on your quest for adventure and glory.\nThanks again, and enjoy your stay in the World of Warcraft!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDiablo Stone Panda Collar Zergling Leash\nStart an item: Thendal Grove Gift Voucher Level 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Both factions Quest ID 92454","cats":["zephras-isle"]}});